&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;POSITION SUMMARY:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Rooms Division Supervisor serves as a primary champion for guest satisfaction, driving exceptional service standards across the Rooms Division. This role centers on creating memorable guest journeys, leading service recovery with empathy, and empowering team members to deliver personalized hospitality. By maintaining seamless communication between front-of-house teams and housekeeping, the Rooms Division Supervisor ensures every guest room and interaction reflects the highest standards of warmth, quality, and care.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Guest Experience &amp;amp; Engagement&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a visible host in the lobby during peak check-in and check-out times to welcome arriving guests, manage flow, and offer personalized assistance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee VIP arrivals, amenity execution, and special requests (anniversaries, birthdays, accessibility needs) to ensure tailored experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Seek new opportunities to add to the guest experience, coordinating with Director of Rooms to create proposals and budgets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively seek out guest feedback, build rapport, and anticipate unstated needs throughout the guest lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor guest feedback platforms (e.g. TripAdvisor, Google Reviews) to identify trends, celebrate successes, and implement service enhancements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Service Recovery &amp;amp; Resolution&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own elevated guest issues and complaints, applying empathy, active listening, and creative problem-solving to turn challenging situations into positive outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Authorize and track service recovery gestures, room upgrades, and amenities within established budget guidelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow up directly with guests who experienced disruptions during their stay to ensure complete satisfaction prior to departure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Operational Coordination &amp;amp; Quality Assurance&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bridge communication between Front Office and Housekeeping to prioritize room assignments, expedite early arrivals, and fulfill guest room preferences seamlessly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee day-to-day operation of Front Office and Housekeeping teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform detailed guest-eye view inspections of rooms, suites, and public areas, evaluating not only cleanliness but comfort, lighting, ambiance, and small hospitality touches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with Engineering/Maintenance to ensure room defects impacting guest comfort are addressed immediately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Team Coaching &amp;amp; Hospitality Culture&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead daily shift huddles focused on service standards, guest recognition programs, and personalized hospitality behaviors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach, mentor, and empower Front Desk and Housekeeping staff to make autonomous decisions that delight guests and resolve concerns on the spot.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct administrative work for Front Office and Housekeeping departments, including scheduling, ordering/inventory management, accounting, and other assignments from the Director of Rooms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct ongoing training on empathy, active listening, cultural awareness, and elevated communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;KEY PERFORMANCE INDICATORS (KPIS)&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Overall Guest Satisfaction / Net Promoter Score (NPS)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Service Recovery Resolution &amp;amp; Retention Rate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guest Room Quality &amp;amp; Hospitality Inspection Scores&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Brand Loyalty Recognition &amp;amp; Amenity Execution Accuracy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS &amp;amp; WORKING CONDITIONS&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to stand, walk, and move throughout the property for extended periods.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility to work varied shifts, including mornings, evenings, weekends, and holidays to align with guest arrival and departure flows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education&lt;/strong&gt;:&amp;nbsp;High School Diploma or equivalent required. A degree or diploma in Hospitality Management or a related field is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;: Minimum three years of experience in a guest-facing role within the hospitality/service industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication and interpersonal skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving and conflict resolution abilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent customer service orientation with a genuine passion for guest satisfaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and time management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in using Property Management Systems (PMS) and other relevant software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently and as part of a team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and accuracy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work flexible hours, including evening, overnight, weekends, and holidays.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are a dynamic and experienced hospitality professional with a passion for delivering exceptional guest experiences, we invite you to join our team as a Rooms Division Supervisor at Nobu Hotel Toronto.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hourly Rate: $31.00&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vacancy Status: Existing Position&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Apply now to be part of a luxury hotel experience that exemplifies excellence in service and hospitality.&lt;/p&gt;
